= Gardens

These are gardens of the #link("https://csszengarden.com/")[digital kind].
They're kind of like this page: a collection of items, usually links, but sometimes images and other rich media.

- #link("/contact/")[Contact]

  - This has all my main contact information along with links to profiles I maintain across the internet.
  
- #link("/people/")[People]

  - #link("https://functor.systems/")[functor.systems] has promised to create a commutative webring of its members at `ring.functor.systems`, but, pending the completion of that arduous project, I've put together a webring of my own (sadly it doesn't #link("https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Commutative_ring")[commute]). This page is a collection of links to other people's personal sites that I find interesting.
  
= Philosophy

Somewhat blog post-like in style, but with less of a focus on a particular concept or idea.
Here, I opt for more general philosophical discussions about broader themes.
Most of these pages elaborate on what's discussed in the #link("/about/")[about] page.

- #link("/academics/")[Academics]

  - I detail my formal and informal academic background and pursuits, with some discussion about what I've learned and links to relevant resources
  
- #link("/computing")[How I do my computing]

  - This is a reference to Richard Stallman's legendary #link("https://stallman.org/stallman-computing.html")[How I do my computing] page. My opinions may not be as serious, and my software is certainly not as dated.
